kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[1]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,pa5,"responses-input-items-have-type","The OpenAI Responses adapter MUST serialize every input item with an explicit type field matching the Responses API schema: message items as {type: message, role, content: [{type: input_text|output_text, text}]}, function calls as {type: function_call, ...}, function outputs as {type: function_call_output, ...}. A bare {role, content} object with no type MUST NOT be emitted: the Responses API rejects such items with Cannot determine type of 'item' once non-message items are mixed into the input array (which happens exactly on a tool-calling continuation round). An assistant round that carries only a tool call and no text MUST NOT emit an empty message item (only the function_call item). Evidence: convert_messages_to_input_items built message items as {role, content} without type, so the first real tool continuation round after the c375 ReAct-loop fix was rejected by OpenAI with Cannot determine type of 'item'; the function had no test coverage.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[2]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  pa5,"every-item-declares-type","a conversation with user assistant tool_call and tool_result messages is converted to Responses input items","the items are inspected","every item has a type field (message or function_call or function_call_output) and message content is an array of typed text parts"
  pa5,"tool-continuation-not-rejected","a tool-calling continuation round request is sent to the Responses API","the request body is the converted items","it is accepted (no Cannot determine type of 'item' error) because every item declares its type"
